{"name":"Artisan Tan","hex":"#b09879","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"artisan","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A skilled manual worker who uses tools and machinery in a particular craft.","A person who displays great dexterity."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Artisanal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/artisan"},{"term":"tan","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["The trigonometric function tangent."]},{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Tangale."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tan"}],"entries":[{"title":"Artisan","blocks":[{"text":"An artisan is a skilled craft worker who makes or creates material objects partly or entirely by hand. These objects may be functional or strictly decorative, for example furniture, decorative art, sculpture, clothing, food items, household items, and tools and mechanisms such as the handmade clockwork movement of a watchmaker. Artisans practice a craft and may through experience and aptitude reach the expressive levels of an artist."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Bessie_Potter_Vonnoh_in_her_studio_by_Jessie_Tarbox_Beals%2C_c._1905_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Bessie_Potter_Vonnoh_in_her_studio_by_Jessie_Tarbox_Beals%2C_c._1905_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artisan","wikidata":"Q1294787"},{"title":"Tan (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Tan is a pale tone of brown. The name is derived from tannum used in the tanning of leather."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Chestnut_Oak_Bark.jpg/330px-Chestnut_Oak_Bark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tan_(color)","wikidata":"Q1670336"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Traditional_Bagh_hand_block_print_master_cra